# Mobile app environment — intentionally contains NO Stripe keys.
#
# This app has no env loader (no react-native-config, no process.env at
# runtime), and it must stay that way for payments:
#
#   * STRIPE_SECRET_KEY must never exist on a client. It can create charges,
#     issue refunds and read every customer's data.
#   * STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is not secret, but it is still not hardcoded here.
#     src/components/payments/StripeBootstrap.tsx fetches it at runtime from
#     GET /payments/config and hands it to <StripeProvider>, so rotating the key
#     or pointing a build at a different Stripe account needs no app release.
#   * STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET is server-side only; the app never sees webhooks.
#
# Card details are collected by Stripe's PaymentSheet, so no card data reaches
# this codebase either.
#
# The backend base URL currently lives in src/services/api.ts (API_BASE_URL).
# If that ever moves into an env file, add its placeholder here — never a key.
